WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:02:16.831 --> 00:02:18.873
Franck, you got news.


00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.456
Here.


00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.873
You better get moving. Okay?


00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.873
Thanks, Cortès.


00:02:33.623 --> 00:02:35.331
Good luck to you, Captain.


00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.956
It devours...


00:03:10.165 --> 00:03:12.081
the purity of innocence.


00:03:14.123 --> 00:03:19.040
By feasting on souls,
he nourishes his power.


00:03:19.206 --> 00:03:21.248
Never invite him in.


00:03:22.415 --> 00:03:25.165
He can invade your home.


00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:30.123
Never answer him lest you fall
into his void.


00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:35.666
For it is in the essence of those
you love that the monster resides.


00:05:52.292 --> 00:05:55.000
The small aircraft carrying
tourists crashed two weeks ago


00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:56.583
in the Gernon Valley.


00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.958
The reason for the crash
remains a mystery.


00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:02.143
The search for the remaining debris from
the plane were called off Sunday night.


00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:05.083
The body of the pilot,
a man in his fifties,


00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:08.875
was found at the site of the crash,
and still has not been identified.


00:06:09.042 --> 00:06:10.792
We're joined now by our special envoy,


00:06:10.958 --> 00:06:12.838
who is reporting live
from the coroner's office,


00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.458
Shit...


00:06:14.625 --> 00:06:15.976
Thank you, Jim.


00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.226
I'm here at the Gernon coroner's office


00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:18.250
where the identity


00:06:18.417 --> 00:06:19.792
of the man remains unknown.


00:06:19.959 --> 00:06:21.418
Fucking hell.


00:06:21.584 --> 00:06:22.894
The dental records


00:06:22.918 --> 00:06:24.251
have not uncovered his identity


00:06:24.418 --> 00:06:26.251
and DNA samples are being analyzed...


00:06:44.584 --> 00:06:46.709
Excuse me. Hey.


00:06:51.084 --> 00:06:52.626
Hello, Ma'am.


00:06:52.793 --> 00:06:54.793
Can't be here, it's dangerous.


00:06:54.959 --> 00:06:56.039
Please go back to your car.


00:06:56.126 --> 00:06:57.459
I want nothing more than


00:06:57.626 --> 00:06:58.918
to get back to my car.


00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:00.334
This gonna take a while?


00:07:00.501 --> 00:07:02.019
If we're not moving fast enough for ya,


00:07:02.043 --> 00:07:03.477
maybe you can help us clear the logs.


00:07:03.501 --> 00:07:04.918
What?


00:07:05.084 --> 00:07:06.501
Not from around here, are ya?


00:07:07.084 --> 00:07:08.918
Just get back in your car.


00:07:09.084 --> 00:07:10.293
Wait like everyone else.


00:07:29.168 --> 00:07:30.751
Thanks for your help back there.


00:07:30.918 --> 00:07:32.293
You're welcome.


00:07:33.668 --> 00:07:36.251
Captain de Roland, National Police Force.


00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:40.793
I have to get to Roquenoire,


00:07:40.959 --> 00:07:42.001
can you drop me off there?


00:07:42.168 --> 00:07:44.209
The National Police Force don't have cars?


00:07:44.376 --> 00:07:45.502
I'm not from here.


00:07:45.669 --> 00:07:47.127
I came by bus.


00:07:48.002 --> 00:07:49.520
A colleague was supposed to pick me up,


00:07:49.544 --> 00:07:51.584
but I'm sure they got
delayed by the roadblock here.


00:07:52.002 --> 00:07:53.252
Where's your uniform?


00:07:54.044 --> 00:07:55.252
I'm a detective.


00:07:55.419 --> 00:07:57.044
Can I see your badge again?


00:07:57.919 --> 00:07:59.879
- Okay, forget it.
- I'll get another car, thanks.


00:08:01.169 --> 00:08:02.835
Alright, get in.


00:08:14.627 --> 00:08:16.502
Just know I can defend myself.


00:08:17.877 --> 00:08:19.460
Won't be necessary.


00:08:21.294 --> 00:08:23.377
What are you here for?


00:08:23.544 --> 00:08:26.919
I'm investigating
a suspicious disappearance case.


00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:29.919
And who has disappeared so suspiciously?


00:08:31.877 --> 00:08:34.127
If you could just drop me
off at this address.


00:08:35.877 --> 00:08:38.377
Um, please.


00:09:08.669 --> 00:09:10.461
You don't wear your seat belt?


00:09:13.628 --> 00:09:15.795
You know, I can write you up for that.


00:09:16.378 --> 00:09:18.711
And I could let you walk
the rest of the way.


00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:33.003
THE SOUL EATER


00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:38.670
Okay. It's right up ahead there.


00:09:54.586 --> 00:09:55.628
Thank you very much.


00:09:57.128 --> 00:09:58.586
Excuse me, what are you doing?


00:09:58.753 --> 00:10:00.545
It's the same address as your GPS.


00:10:09.836 --> 00:10:12.545
- Chief Marcelin.
- Are you Inspector Guardiano?


00:10:12.711 --> 00:10:15.378
Yes, and this is Captain de Roland
of the National Police Force.


00:10:15.545 --> 00:10:17.170
Evening, Chief.


00:10:17.336 --> 00:10:19.920
We're a bit late covering the
perimeter and securing the scene.


00:10:20.086 --> 00:10:22.711
I only have two men available,
and with this nightmare...


00:10:22.878 --> 00:10:23.920
we could use a lot more.


00:10:24.086 --> 00:10:25.170
Hey, Tauraud!


00:10:25.336 --> 00:10:28.045
- Where's my goddamn light?
- Coming, Chief.


00:10:28.211 --> 00:10:30.295
And check out the back
of the house for me.


00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:35.212
- What?
- Nothing.


00:10:35.379 --> 00:10:36.962
You never asked me anything.


00:10:37.129 --> 00:10:38.921
No problem, Inspector.


00:10:39.421 --> 00:10:41.587
A good investigator would have grilled me.


00:10:42.379 --> 00:10:44.379
- Alright, look.
- I'm not gonna get caught up


00:10:44.546 --> 00:10:46.129
in any cliche cop bullshit.


00:10:46.296 --> 00:10:48.647
I'm only here to see if the missing kids
have anything to do


00:10:48.671 --> 00:10:50.046
with your crime scene.


00:10:50.212 --> 00:10:51.546
Inspector.


00:10:51.712 --> 00:10:52.837
Coming.


00:10:54.504 --> 00:10:55.754
Be right there.


00:10:57.712 --> 00:10:59.796
Gonnet, Inspector Guardiano.


00:11:00.629 --> 00:11:03.171
Here, you better put these on,
you're gonna need them.


00:11:03.337 --> 00:11:05.004
Sorry we got nothing for the smell.


00:11:19.337 --> 00:11:21.921
Just a warning, this isn't very pretty.


00:11:27.546 --> 00:11:29.462
Nobody told you about this butchery.


00:11:30.212 --> 00:11:32.254
Not specifically, no.


00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:21.047
You want my advice?


00:12:21.213 --> 00:12:22.963
This is what I think happened.


00:12:23.547 --> 00:12:25.297
The Vasseurs were having their breakfast


00:12:25.463 --> 00:12:28.297
and an argument started that quickly
turned into a violent rage


00:12:28.463 --> 00:12:31.797
and they killed each other with whatever
they could get their hands on.


00:12:34.172 --> 00:12:37.797
It's strange that there are
no defensive wounds on their arms.


00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:42.422
So they attack each other and they don't
even defend themselves?


00:12:49.463 --> 00:12:51.547
What can you tell me about the Vasseurs?


00:12:52.672 --> 00:12:54.255
There's not a whole lot to tell.


00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:57.880
She worked at the bakery,
and he was unemployed.


00:12:58.047 --> 00:13:01.213
They had a 12-year-old named
Evan, but no one can find him.


00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.922
- What?
- We looked everywhere,


00:13:03.088 --> 00:13:04.130
but never found him.


00:13:05.088 --> 00:13:06.481
Make sure you tell Captain de Roland.


00:13:06.505 --> 00:13:07.880
He'll want to know.


00:13:08.547 --> 00:13:11.588
Anyway, nothing indicates there was
a third person here when it happened.


00:13:11.755 --> 00:13:13.898
And with all this blood,
we'd find traces of something,


00:13:13.922 --> 00:13:16.130
and the doors and windows
were locked from the inside.


00:13:16.963 --> 00:13:19.172
So they prepared this nice breakfast


00:13:19.338 --> 00:13:20.797
then it's carnage.


00:13:20.963 --> 00:13:22.088
Makes no sense.


00:15:04.382 --> 00:15:06.590
Police,


00:15:06.757 --> 00:15:08.465
show yourself.


00:15:30.174 --> 00:15:31.424
Hey.


00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:33.424
No, it's alright, sweetie. Okay?


00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:35.090
Don't worry, it's all good.


00:15:35.257 --> 00:15:36.507
I'm with the police.


00:15:36.674 --> 00:15:38.340
You're Evan, right?


00:15:38.507 --> 00:15:39.799
My name's Elisabeth.


00:15:39.965 --> 00:15:41.257
He was here.


00:15:41.882 --> 00:15:43.424
Who was here?


00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:45.007
The Soul Eater.


00:15:45.174 --> 00:15:46.549
What are you saying?


00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:50.757
The Soul Eater.


00:16:24.425 --> 00:16:26.258
So you looked everywhere?


00:16:29.966 --> 00:16:31.466
Don't look.


00:16:38.008 --> 00:16:39.591
Call the hospital.


00:16:54.758 --> 00:16:56.966
We need am ambulance at the Vasseur house.


00:16:57.133 --> 00:16:58.484
Copy that, Unit 12.


00:16:58.508 --> 00:16:59.758
Specify what it's for?


00:16:59.925 --> 00:17:01.734
They found the kid, and he's in shock.


00:17:01.758 --> 00:17:04.118
Copy that, sending am ambulance right now.


00:17:12.591 --> 00:17:14.508
Justine, 9 years old.


00:17:14.675 --> 00:17:17.258
Mila, 10.


00:17:17.425 --> 00:17:19.216
Megan, 9.


00:17:19.883 --> 00:17:21.841
Anthony, 10.


00:17:22.008 --> 00:17:24.300
Lucy, 11.


00:17:25.466 --> 00:17:26.591
Raphaël...


00:17:28.425 --> 00:17:29.716
- 10.
- Police stations


00:17:29.883 --> 00:17:31.925
have tons of pictures like these.


00:17:32.091 --> 00:17:33.091
When did they go missing?


00:17:33.216 --> 00:17:35.216
First one dates back about six months.


00:17:36.175 --> 00:17:38.801
All of these kids disappeared
into neighbouring towns.


00:17:38.967 --> 00:17:40.342
Located in the valley.


00:17:41.009 --> 00:17:43.342
We don't have any serious leads
except for a white van


00:17:43.509 --> 00:17:45.443
that witnesses say was spotted
at the time they went missing.


00:17:45.467 --> 00:17:46.676
No make or model?


00:17:46.842 --> 00:17:48.967
No, just a simple white van.


00:17:49.467 --> 00:17:52.842
But all those towns are connected by the
same grid in their surveillance cameras.


00:17:53.009 --> 00:17:55.277
And you checked all the plates
belonging to a white van?


00:17:55.301 --> 00:17:59.217
Yeah, we started by looking
into everyone who has a criminal record.


00:17:59.384 --> 00:18:01.259
Everyone who lives in the area.


00:18:01.426 --> 00:18:02.676
We got nothing.


00:18:03.342 --> 00:18:06.509
We even looked
into partial and fake plates.


00:18:07.467 --> 00:18:09.092
Still came up empty.


00:18:09.884 --> 00:18:11.051
Hoping for a miracle.


00:18:12.967 --> 00:18:15.301
And the miracle
was the Vasseurs van, right?


00:18:16.259 --> 00:18:17.634
I don't know.


00:18:18.176 --> 00:18:19.634
I was hoping...


00:18:19.801 --> 00:18:21.259
when we find a suspect vehicle


00:18:21.426 --> 00:18:22.842
on the scene of a double homicide,


00:18:23.009 --> 00:18:24.509
we start asking questions.


00:18:25.092 --> 00:18:26.717
And maybe believe in miracles.


00:18:26.884 --> 00:18:30.634
Franck, I'm gonna be straight with you.


00:18:30.801 --> 00:18:33.342
This double-homicide case here,


00:18:33.509 --> 00:18:35.801
I was the one who asked for it.


00:18:35.967 --> 00:18:37.717
And I'm gonna be the one who's running it.


00:18:37.884 --> 00:18:39.842
That was also a request I made.


00:18:40.509 --> 00:18:42.467
We won't be a team.


00:18:42.634 --> 00:18:44.551
We might share a meal or a hotel,


00:18:44.717 --> 00:18:46.676
- but not this case.
- You take the murders,


00:18:46.842 --> 00:18:47.985
I'll take the disappearances.


00:18:48.009 --> 00:18:49.884
Alright, we got a deal.


00:18:55.051 --> 00:18:56.551
Good night, Franck.


00:19:02.552 --> 00:19:05.218
He comes with the mist and the storm.


00:19:05.385 --> 00:19:08.718
He breathes his madness
on both men and beasts.


00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:11.052
If you hear whispers in the forest


00:19:11.218 --> 00:19:13.135
and cries in the mountains,


00:19:13.718 --> 00:19:16.760
the infamous monster has awakened.


00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:20.427
He's here to devour your soul.


00:19:46.843 --> 00:19:50.343
WELCOME TO ROQUENOIR
RUN


00:21:01.678 --> 00:21:03.303
Excuse me.


00:21:03.469 --> 00:21:05.362
Did you happen to see
someone coming out before me?


00:21:05.386 --> 00:21:06.969
No one's come out before you, sir


00:21:11.053 --> 00:21:12.261
Elisabeth.


00:21:12.428 --> 00:21:15.053
- Somebody got...
- I don't want to know about it.


00:21:15.219 --> 00:21:17.419
But you should know that we came out
empty with the van.


00:21:17.469 --> 00:21:19.678
No traces of blood, no fingerprints.


00:21:20.678 --> 00:21:23.428
Sorry, Franck, that's the end
of the line for you.


00:21:31.969 --> 00:21:34.928
MUNICIPAL POLICE


00:21:39.886 --> 00:21:41.178
Morning, Inspector.


00:21:41.344 --> 00:21:42.719
Pascale Minot, Mayor of Roquenoir.


00:21:42.886 --> 00:21:43.886
- Hello.
- You know,


00:21:44.011 --> 00:21:45.303
this is a quiet little town


00:21:45.469 --> 00:21:46.909
so when something like this happens,


00:21:47.053 --> 00:21:48.303
everyone talks about it.


00:21:48.469 --> 00:21:49.761
And people get scared.


00:21:49.928 --> 00:21:51.248
I can assure you, Madame Mayor,


00:21:51.386 --> 00:21:52.804
I am scared, too.


00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:55.012
But of your local cops.


00:21:56.137 --> 00:21:58.345
A child is found a few metres
from the crime scene,


00:21:58.512 --> 00:21:59.929
and you walk right by him?


00:22:00.095 --> 00:22:01.345
For several hours?


00:22:01.512 --> 00:22:03.472
Excuse me, Inspector,
but like I said yesterday,


00:22:03.554 --> 00:22:05.304
I looked in the basement
and found nothing.


00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:06.679
Heard nothing.


00:22:07.595 --> 00:22:08.738
As you know, we're understaffed.


00:22:08.762 --> 00:22:10.220
And I had other things to deal with.


00:22:10.387 --> 00:22:11.887
Seriously?


00:22:12.054 --> 00:22:14.054
- Are we done here?
- We did what we could, okay?


00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:15.980
Were we overwhelmed
with what happened, sure,


00:22:16.137 --> 00:22:17.512
but we can't go back and fix it.


00:22:17.679 --> 00:22:19.196
This sort of thing happens all the time.


00:22:19.220 --> 00:22:21.387
People come here from their big cities,


00:22:21.554 --> 00:22:22.929
and tell us how to run things.


00:22:23.095 --> 00:22:24.655
And you're not the first one to come here


00:22:24.679 --> 00:22:26.512
and tell us what we should've
done, Inspector.


00:22:27.929 --> 00:22:31.137
Fifteen days ago, a small tourist plane
crashed here in the mountains.


00:22:31.304 --> 00:22:32.784
And people like you from the big city


00:22:32.929 --> 00:22:34.409
were very happy to send us local folk


00:22:34.512 --> 00:22:36.345
to search through the wreck for them.


00:22:37.762 --> 00:22:40.387
Yes. Yes, yes,
it's me.


00:22:42.179 --> 00:22:43.679
I'll call you back.


00:22:44.429 --> 00:22:46.595
Marcelin, we've got work to do.


00:22:47.429 --> 00:22:49.238
Find me everything there is
to find on the Vasseurs.


00:22:49.262 --> 00:22:50.345
I want it all.


00:22:50.512 --> 00:22:51.512
I'm going to the morgue.


00:22:51.679 --> 00:22:53.012
We've got news on the bodies.


00:22:53.179 --> 00:22:54.780
I guess there's something else we missed.


00:22:54.804 --> 00:22:56.095
Inspector.


00:22:56.262 --> 00:22:58.102
There's a proper bitch
if I've ever seen one.


00:23:01.845 --> 00:23:04.512
Um, the two of us seem to have
gotten off on the wrong foot.


00:23:04.679 --> 00:23:06.845
We've had a lot to deal with here,


00:23:07.012 --> 00:23:09.387
and I suppose we've become
leary of strangers.


00:23:10.262 --> 00:23:13.262
Before all this, Roquenoir
was a charming little town.


00:23:13.429 --> 00:23:16.512
Thanks mostly to our world-renowned
health centre and spa.


00:23:17.263 --> 00:23:19.447
But since the construction of
the highway through the valley,


00:23:19.471 --> 00:23:20.763
no one stops here.


00:23:21.388 --> 00:23:24.721
So the spa and health centre shut down
and the local businesses, well...


00:23:24.888 --> 00:23:27.305
Roquenoir pretty much became a ghost town.


00:23:27.930 --> 00:23:30.846
And every year, I have to fight to keep
the school open.


00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:33.638
So whoever could leave, left, and...


00:23:34.680 --> 00:23:37.805
Whoever chose to stay is just trying to...


00:23:37.971 --> 00:23:39.138
Survive?


00:23:40.263 --> 00:23:41.930
Exactly right.


00:23:42.846 --> 00:23:43.971
Alright, look.


00:23:44.138 --> 00:23:45.346
I'm here to solve a crime,


00:23:45.513 --> 00:23:46.713
and whether we like it or not,


00:23:46.763 --> 00:23:47.971
we're all on the same side.


00:23:48.138 --> 00:23:49.638
But what crime, Inspector?


00:23:49.805 --> 00:23:52.221
I thought that the Vasseurs
killed each other.


00:23:52.680 --> 00:23:56.180
Listen, there are no killers
in Roquenoir, alright?


00:23:56.346 --> 00:23:58.638
So just go back home, Inspector.


00:23:58.805 --> 00:24:01.471
And deal with your personal issues.


00:24:24.305 --> 00:24:27.305
LA FONTAINE HOSPITAL


00:24:30.263 --> 00:24:32.430
- It's right here, Captain.
- Thank you.


00:24:34.596 --> 00:24:37.388
Sir, can I help you?


00:24:37.930 --> 00:24:41.639
Yes, Captain de Roland, National Police.


00:24:41.806 --> 00:24:43.639
I need to speak to Evan Vasseur.


00:24:44.847 --> 00:24:46.681
I'm sorry, Captain.


00:24:47.306 --> 00:24:48.472
But it's too soon.


00:24:49.681 --> 00:24:51.847
Evan just suffered something
very traumatic.


00:24:52.014 --> 00:24:53.264
He needs to rest more.


00:24:53.431 --> 00:24:55.431
It's important. An emergency.


00:24:56.181 --> 00:24:57.264
You are?


00:24:57.431 --> 00:24:59.347
Carole Marbas, child psychiatrist.


00:24:59.514 --> 00:25:02.681
I'm investigating the disappearance
of minors and he could help me.


00:25:02.847 --> 00:25:04.097
Can I see him?


00:25:04.264 --> 00:25:05.389
No, 'fraid not.


00:25:05.889 --> 00:25:07.389
This child is fragile.


00:25:08.597 --> 00:25:09.639
I'll come by later then.


00:25:09.806 --> 00:25:10.972
Sure.


00:25:11.764 --> 00:25:13.306
Goodbye, Doctor.


00:25:48.972 --> 00:25:51.347
Shit, this isn't the time, Cortes.


00:26:30.848 --> 00:26:32.473
Hello, Evan.


00:26:37.515 --> 00:26:38.932
My name is Franck.


00:26:41.432 --> 00:26:42.848
I'm a policeman.


00:26:46.140 --> 00:26:48.473
I'd love to have a chat
with you if that's alright.


00:26:50.265 --> 00:26:51.557
What do you say?


00:26:54.973 --> 00:26:56.723
Very sorry about your parents.


00:26:57.640 --> 00:26:59.223
You're a liar.


00:26:59.390 --> 00:27:01.432
I can hear it in your voice.


00:27:04.890 --> 00:27:07.390
Evan, I'm really sad for you.


00:27:16.140 --> 00:27:17.973
Here's what I'm proposing.


00:27:18.765 --> 00:27:21.348
We won't talk about
what happened yesterday.


00:27:22.098 --> 00:27:24.265
We'll just play a little game.


00:27:24.432 --> 00:27:26.140
It's a yes or no game.


00:27:27.307 --> 00:27:28.932
You know it?


00:27:32.599 --> 00:27:36.266
I ask you some questions and you reply.


00:27:37.099 --> 00:27:38.516
With yes or no.


00:27:49.433 --> 00:27:51.683
The white van that's in the garage,


00:27:51.849 --> 00:27:53.558
does it belong to your parents?


00:27:54.891 --> 00:27:56.683
Yeah.


00:27:59.349 --> 00:28:00.933
Look at these pictures.


00:28:01.766 --> 00:28:03.016
Do you know any of these kids?


00:28:03.641 --> 00:28:05.141
Have you seen them before?


00:28:14.141 --> 00:28:15.516
Have you ever seen them?


00:28:18.516 --> 00:28:19.974
Yeah.


00:28:21.099 --> 00:28:22.599
All six?


00:28:22.766 --> 00:28:23.808
Yeah.


00:28:25.349 --> 00:28:26.933
Know where they are?


00:28:27.766 --> 00:28:29.474
Don't you know?


00:28:29.641 --> 00:28:30.933
No, I don't.


00:28:31.516 --> 00:28:32.849
I'm looking for them.


00:28:42.933 --> 00:28:44.683
Are they dead?


00:28:45.808 --> 00:28:46.974
Yeah.


00:28:48.683 --> 00:28:50.016
All of them?


00:28:51.058 --> 00:28:52.308
Yeah.


00:28:59.559 --> 00:29:01.350
You know who hurt those kids, Evan?


00:29:02.184 --> 00:29:03.475
The Soul Eater.


00:29:04.600 --> 00:29:06.392
And, who's the Soul Eater?


00:29:08.059 --> 00:29:10.684
He's here.


00:29:11.850 --> 00:29:13.142
Evan?


00:29:13.309 --> 00:29:14.392
Evan!


00:29:35.100 --> 00:29:36.475
Get out of here.


00:29:36.642 --> 00:29:37.850
Immediately.


00:29:39.392 --> 00:29:40.767
Out now!


00:29:54.642 --> 00:29:56.142
You okay, Evan?


00:29:58.892 --> 00:30:00.225
What did you say?


00:30:32.851 --> 00:30:35.518
Okay, I've never seen
anything like this, Inspector.


00:30:35.685 --> 00:30:38.393
I counted 81 entry wounds
on the body of the woman


00:30:38.560 --> 00:30:40.060
and 73 on her husband.


00:30:40.226 --> 00:30:42.685
Most of the wounds were inflicted
with broken glass, forks,


00:30:42.851 --> 00:30:44.643
and especially kitchen knives.


00:30:45.226 --> 00:30:47.268
I found human flesh between their teeth


00:30:47.435 --> 00:30:49.018
and in their esophagus.


00:30:49.393 --> 00:30:51.810
Wait, are you saying
they actually ate each other?


00:30:51.976 --> 00:30:53.101
Yeah, you could say that.


00:30:55.101 --> 00:30:57.643
You think it's possible someone else
might have done this?


00:30:58.393 --> 00:31:00.893
No, and I'm very certain on that point.


00:31:01.060 --> 00:31:03.143
It was easy enough
to reconstruct the fight.


00:31:03.310 --> 00:31:05.060
They very clearly attacked each other.


00:31:06.185 --> 00:31:07.935
- So who died first?
- She did.


00:31:08.101 --> 00:31:11.226
But the disturbing thing is that the man
continued stabbing his wife


00:31:11.393 --> 00:31:12.935
long after she was already dead.


00:31:13.101 --> 00:31:15.268
Then he started stabbing himself.


00:31:16.143 --> 00:31:19.351
But it's just... No one commits suicide
by stabbing themselves


00:31:19.518 --> 00:31:21.601
so randomly like that. It's...


00:31:22.060 --> 00:31:24.643
I don't get it.
It doesn't make any sense.


00:31:32.518 --> 00:31:34.185
Inspector?


00:31:35.018 --> 00:31:36.643
Inspector? Are you alright?


00:31:37.810 --> 00:31:38.851
Yeah, yeah, I'm good.


00:31:39.018 --> 00:31:40.018
Thanks.


00:31:40.143 --> 00:31:41.643
Can you get all this to me


00:31:41.810 --> 00:31:42.810
in writing, please.


00:31:42.935 --> 00:31:44.095
- Yes, of course.
- Thank you.


00:31:44.185 --> 00:31:45.519
Do you have another five minutes?


00:31:45.686 --> 00:31:47.602
I saved the best part for last.


00:31:47.769 --> 00:31:48.769
Go ahead.


00:31:48.936 --> 00:31:50.102
The couple had an orgasm


00:31:50.269 --> 00:31:51.311
while killing each other.


00:31:51.477 --> 00:31:52.686
I found in their underwear


00:31:52.852 --> 00:31:55.436
traces of sperm and vaginal secretions.


00:32:11.602 --> 00:32:13.436
Excuse me, hello, Ma'am.


00:32:17.227 --> 00:32:18.311
Can I help you?


00:32:18.477 --> 00:32:20.352
Yes.


00:32:20.519 --> 00:32:22.269
Captain de Roland, National Police.


00:32:22.436 --> 00:32:23.436
Fuck.


00:32:23.561 --> 00:32:25.078
I have a few quick questions for you,


00:32:25.102 --> 00:32:27.519
either you answer them now
and get it over with,


00:32:27.977 --> 00:32:30.352
or, I can take you down to the station


00:32:30.519 --> 00:32:33.159
when it's convenient for me and detain
you there as long as I want.


00:32:33.227 --> 00:32:34.227
It's up to you.


00:32:35.061 --> 00:32:36.186
What do you want?


00:32:36.352 --> 00:32:38.019
It's concerning your neighbours,


00:32:38.186 --> 00:32:39.186
the Vasseurs.


00:32:39.852 --> 00:32:41.852
I told the police everything yesterday.


00:32:42.019 --> 00:32:43.686
Well, that was them and not me.


00:32:49.852 --> 00:32:51.852
Is it true they killed each other?


00:32:52.019 --> 00:32:53.102
Who told you that?


00:32:53.269 --> 00:32:54.977
People talk here.


00:32:55.144 --> 00:32:56.394
This is Roquenoir.


00:32:56.561 --> 00:32:58.936
There's no hiding anything in this town.


00:32:59.519 --> 00:33:00.852
And...


00:33:01.019 --> 00:33:02.227
Did you know them well?


00:33:02.394 --> 00:33:04.394
Nobody knew them that well.


00:33:04.561 --> 00:33:06.227
They were weird, didn't talk.


00:33:06.394 --> 00:33:10.395
She... She was timid behind
her counter at the bakery,


00:33:10.562 --> 00:33:11.895
And he...


00:33:12.062 --> 00:33:13.353
Rarely saw him.


00:33:13.520 --> 00:33:15.603
Do you know if they use
their white van very often?


00:33:15.770 --> 00:33:17.704
What are these questions
and why are you asking me?


00:33:17.728 --> 00:33:18.728
Just wondering.


00:33:18.853 --> 00:33:20.770
Never seen them do anything strange?


00:33:21.687 --> 00:33:23.353
Stranger than their kid?


00:33:24.062 --> 00:33:25.978
They've got a totally weird kid.


00:33:26.145 --> 00:33:29.478
He sees all kinds of monsters and spirits.


00:33:30.478 --> 00:33:32.312
I've seen him talking to himself.


00:33:33.978 --> 00:33:35.728
I'm pretty sure he killed my dog.


00:33:35.895 --> 00:33:37.062
Wait, what?


00:33:37.228 --> 00:33:38.937
My dog used to run onto their lawn


00:33:39.103 --> 00:33:41.270
and a few days ago
he took off and never came back.


00:33:41.437 --> 00:33:42.853
And did you make a complaint?


00:33:43.020 --> 00:33:45.437
No. The cops around here are idiots.


00:33:49.520 --> 00:33:51.062
Have you ever seen these kids before?


00:33:51.228 --> 00:33:52.353
Nina!


00:33:52.520 --> 00:33:54.770
They all went missing in the area.


00:33:57.103 --> 00:33:58.687
- What's going on, Nina?
- Nothing.


00:33:58.853 --> 00:34:00.520
- Hi there, sir.
- Who're you?


00:34:00.687 --> 00:34:02.562
Arnaud, please, he's a cop.


00:34:03.187 --> 00:34:05.562
- A police officer.
- And why do I give a fuck?


00:34:06.978 --> 00:34:08.103
What's all this here?


00:34:08.270 --> 00:34:10.478
These are kids
who've gone missing in the area.


00:34:12.978 --> 00:34:14.603
Have you seen them before?


00:34:14.770 --> 00:34:15.937
Sorry.


00:34:16.520 --> 00:34:18.270
Hey, man. What the fuck?


00:34:18.437 --> 00:34:19.770
- What are you?
- Let him go!


00:34:19.937 --> 00:34:21.687
Fucking shit! Arnaud, get inside.


00:34:21.853 --> 00:34:23.312
Go inside, are you fucking crazy?


00:34:23.478 --> 00:34:25.329
Why are you talking
to that piece of shit cop?


00:34:25.353 --> 00:34:26.562
Why'd you open the...


00:35:38.771 --> 00:35:40.104
Are you out of your mind?


00:35:40.271 --> 00:35:41.813
Do you want to get yourself killed?


00:35:41.979 --> 00:35:44.021
I didn't know you'd be here.


00:35:45.188 --> 00:35:47.021
What are you doing here?


00:35:50.146 --> 00:35:52.438
The Vasseurs were spying on their son?


00:35:53.271 --> 00:35:55.146
I asked Evan a few questions this morning.


00:35:55.313 --> 00:35:57.247
Yeah, I know. I just got back
from the hospital.


00:35:57.271 --> 00:35:59.122
And because of your stupidity,
I couldn't talk to him.


00:35:59.146 --> 00:36:01.772
I was pretty clear, Franck.
Evan is my witness.


00:36:02.939 --> 00:36:04.772
Did he tell you anything at least?


00:36:04.939 --> 00:36:06.979
No, not really. He was still
pretty much in shock.


00:36:07.064 --> 00:36:08.230
He kept talking about some...


00:36:08.397 --> 00:36:09.647
Yeah, the Soul Eater. I know.


00:36:09.814 --> 00:36:11.439
That's all he talks about.


00:36:12.022 --> 00:36:13.939
That doesn't explain why you're here.


00:36:14.730 --> 00:36:16.855
I'm looking for the truth just like you.


00:36:17.022 --> 00:36:19.540
I figured that it was possible that
the Vasseurs were responsible


00:36:19.564 --> 00:36:20.689
for taking the missing kids.


00:36:20.855 --> 00:36:22.689
You're completely obsessed, Franck.


00:36:23.189 --> 00:36:24.522
What are you?


00:36:26.689 --> 00:36:28.105
With your double murder.


00:36:28.272 --> 00:36:29.855
They killed each other.


00:36:31.022 --> 00:36:34.397
Nine out of ten cops would've closed
this case, no questions asked.


00:36:34.564 --> 00:36:35.939
But deep inside,


00:36:36.105 --> 00:36:37.456
you have this little voice telling you


00:36:37.480 --> 00:36:39.064
there's something else. Am I wrong?


00:36:39.230 --> 00:36:40.272
Yeah.


00:36:40.439 --> 00:36:41.879
I'm convinced there was someone else


00:36:41.980 --> 00:36:43.060
there when it all happened.


00:36:43.189 --> 00:36:44.522
- Right.
- And you?


00:36:44.689 --> 00:36:45.689
What do you think?


00:36:47.064 --> 00:36:49.397
He was covered in hematomas,
he was abused.


00:36:52.564 --> 00:36:54.230
You don't find this room strange at all?


00:36:58.855 --> 00:37:01.314
I've never seen any kid's room
this neat and tiny.


00:37:01.480 --> 00:37:04.105
- Exactly.
- No kid ever lived in here.


00:37:22.022 --> 00:37:23.772
Here's where I found him.


00:37:28.981 --> 00:37:31.565
And what did your little voice tell ya?


00:37:31.731 --> 00:37:34.023
That his parents kept
him down here to protect him?


00:37:34.940 --> 00:37:37.106
Before ripping each other apart?


00:37:39.065 --> 00:37:41.440
I'm not assuming anything right now.


00:37:52.898 --> 00:37:55.273
Guardiano, check this out.


00:38:00.356 --> 00:38:01.940
Fuck me.


00:38:06.731 --> 00:38:08.440
This is his room.


00:38:08.606 --> 00:38:10.815
I'll put it a call to Child Service.


00:38:11.606 --> 00:38:14.815
I'm going to his school. Somebody
there must have known his situation.


00:38:22.148 --> 00:38:23.690
Soul Eater?


00:38:32.148 --> 00:38:33.815
The Soul Eater.


00:38:34.356 --> 00:38:36.731
It's weird that there are no references
to it on the net.


00:38:36.898 --> 00:38:38.898
As if it doesn't even exist.


00:38:39.065 --> 00:38:41.190
What if it only exists here?


00:38:52.816 --> 00:38:53.857
What's that?


00:38:54.024 --> 00:38:55.107
Nothing interesting.


00:38:55.274 --> 00:38:56.316
An unpaid invoice


00:38:56.482 --> 00:38:57.566
for computer equipment.


00:39:00.107 --> 00:39:01.399
What?


00:39:02.524 --> 00:39:03.649
Computer.


00:39:03.816 --> 00:39:05.649
You guys seized a computer last night?


00:39:05.816 --> 00:39:06.941
No.


00:39:08.816 --> 00:39:10.441
Excuse me, it's my commissioner.


00:39:10.607 --> 00:39:11.941
Hello?


00:39:20.441 --> 00:39:22.732
Yes, I know,
I should've called you earlier.


00:39:25.232 --> 00:39:27.024
I had no information to give you.


00:39:27.774 --> 00:39:29.357
Well, you know, things are slower here.


00:39:30.107 --> 00:39:31.149
As for the pathologist,


00:39:31.316 --> 00:39:32.716
she can only give me final results.


00:39:32.774 --> 00:39:34.607
Or at least, that's what she told me.


00:39:35.649 --> 00:39:37.024
Hang on, I'll call you back.


00:39:43.691 --> 00:39:45.066
Franck!


00:39:46.107 --> 00:39:47.732
Franck, come here!


00:39:47.899 --> 00:39:49.191
Franck!


00:39:51.732 --> 00:39:53.399
- The hell is that?
- I don't know,


00:39:53.566 --> 00:39:54.806
but there's something under it.


00:40:08.607 --> 00:40:10.274
Fuck...


00:40:13.983 --> 00:40:15.358
It's a dog.


00:40:15.900 --> 00:40:17.067
It's the neighbour's.


00:40:17.233 --> 00:40:19.900
Why do you know more
about my case than I do?


00:40:20.067 --> 00:40:21.483
Because it's the same one.


00:40:21.650 --> 00:40:22.858
Excuse me.


00:40:24.275 --> 00:40:25.942
Yes.


00:40:26.108 --> 00:40:27.358
Okay, be right there.


00:40:27.525 --> 00:40:28.845
No, no, it's fine. I'll find you.


00:40:30.400 --> 00:40:32.108
Let's go. Marcelin's waiting for us.


00:40:32.275 --> 00:40:34.608
- Why?
- There's another body.


00:40:54.858 --> 00:40:59.483
DROCOURT SAWMILL


00:41:13.192 --> 00:41:14.858
Inspector.


00:41:15.025 --> 00:41:16.817
- Captain.
- Marcelin.


00:41:16.983 --> 00:41:19.192
- Another ugly one.
- Let's go.


00:41:21.942 --> 00:41:23.650
Be careful where you step.


00:41:31.900 --> 00:41:33.317
It's the owner of the sawmill.


00:41:33.483 --> 00:41:36.525
Yannick Drocourt, 43,
unmarried, and no children.


00:41:37.400 --> 00:41:39.151
It was a successful business.


00:41:39.318 --> 00:41:41.443
No enemies or any problems
that we know of.


00:41:41.609 --> 00:41:43.109
At least, at first glance.


00:41:43.651 --> 00:41:45.318
Like the Vasseurs.


00:41:48.443 --> 00:41:49.859
Who found him?


00:41:50.693 --> 00:41:52.818
It was Henry Maublanc who called it in.


00:41:52.984 --> 00:41:54.318
He's still here in the office.


00:41:54.484 --> 00:41:56.318
I told him to stay
so you could question him.


00:41:56.484 --> 00:41:59.401
Just a warning, though,
he's still pretty freaked out.


00:42:00.276 --> 00:42:02.109
He didn't do this to himself.


00:42:02.859 --> 00:42:03.901
How could he have?


00:42:04.068 --> 00:42:06.026
Swigs back a beer and saws himself in two?


00:42:06.193 --> 00:42:07.609
Marcelin,


00:42:07.776 --> 00:42:09.276
hand me one of your gloves, please.


00:42:10.859 --> 00:42:12.109
Thanks.


00:42:18.859 --> 00:42:20.734
What is this?


00:42:25.609 --> 00:42:27.193
Let's go see this witness.


00:42:40.359 --> 00:42:43.734
I was going back there to pick up
a few planks that I had ordered.


00:42:46.109 --> 00:42:48.401
This morning I called and...


00:42:48.568 --> 00:42:50.693
asked if my order was gonna be ready.


00:42:51.651 --> 00:42:54.151
But there was no answer.


00:42:54.818 --> 00:42:57.859
I left him several messages,
which he never replied to.


00:42:58.776 --> 00:43:01.234
Since I was starting to get a bit worried,


00:43:04.027 --> 00:43:05.985
I decided I'd just come by.


00:43:10.069 --> 00:43:11.610
That's when I found him there.


00:43:16.110 --> 00:43:17.860
Did you know Mr. Drocourt well?


00:43:18.527 --> 00:43:19.902
No.


00:43:22.402 --> 00:43:24.282
And did you see
anyone else when you got here?


00:43:24.444 --> 00:43:25.860
No.


00:43:26.402 --> 00:43:27.902
Didn't notice any other cars?


00:43:28.735 --> 00:43:30.069
No, I didn't.


00:43:32.902 --> 00:43:36.360
- Well, we'll let you go now.
- My colleague has all your information.


00:43:36.527 --> 00:43:38.319
We may have other questions for you


00:43:38.485 --> 00:43:40.819
so please don't leave Roquenoir
for a few days.


00:43:47.652 --> 00:43:49.569
Found this in the Vasseur's van.


00:43:49.735 --> 00:43:52.069
I didn't think it was
very important 'til now.


00:43:52.235 --> 00:43:54.628
Like you said, we can't start a war
between our departments


00:43:54.652 --> 00:43:56.194
by hiding clues from each other.


00:43:56.360 --> 00:43:57.485
Yes, Inspector.


00:43:58.402 --> 00:43:59.819
They're not exactly the same.


00:43:59.985 --> 00:44:01.777
No, but it was made by the same person.


00:44:01.944 --> 00:44:03.420
- It looks like, yeah.
- The ambulance


00:44:03.444 --> 00:44:05.110
will be coming soon to pick up the body.


00:44:06.319 --> 00:44:08.194
Marcelin, you ever heard anyone talk


00:44:08.360 --> 00:44:09.902
about a Soul Eater?


00:44:11.444 --> 00:44:12.610
Yeah.


00:44:15.069 --> 00:44:17.027
All of us grew up hearing that story.


00:44:18.194 --> 00:44:22.027
They told it to us so that we
wouldn't go play up in the mountains.


00:44:22.777 --> 00:44:25.069
Was our version of The Boogeyman.


00:44:25.235 --> 00:44:27.360
A local legend. Why do you ask?


00:44:27.527 --> 00:44:29.195
We found nothing on the net.


00:44:29.861 --> 00:44:31.861
What's this local legend all about?


00:44:32.945 --> 00:44:35.145
About a creature who lives
in the forest, engulfs you,


00:44:35.236 --> 00:44:38.236
if you believe that,
transforms you into a demon.


00:44:38.403 --> 00:44:39.861
And when you return home,


00:44:40.028 --> 00:44:42.236
you still have the same appearance,


00:44:42.403 --> 00:44:43.695
but you're not the same person.


00:44:45.278 --> 00:44:46.778
And you're missing something, a soul.


00:44:46.945 --> 00:44:49.212
If there is someone behind
all the shit going down here,


00:44:49.236 --> 00:44:50.695
they surely know the story.


00:44:52.361 --> 00:44:54.611
Could this figurine
possibly be the Soul Eater?


00:44:54.778 --> 00:44:56.361
Yeah, it's possible.


00:44:56.528 --> 00:44:58.421
But the description's different
depending on the family.


00:44:58.445 --> 00:44:59.805
Everyone sees something different.


00:45:00.528 --> 00:45:01.528
Check out the church.


00:45:01.695 --> 00:45:03.087
The priest actually has a book on him.


00:45:03.111 --> 00:45:04.736
Hang on to this.


00:45:09.403 --> 00:45:10.903
You okay, Captain?


00:45:11.736 --> 00:45:13.820
Not too crazy working with Guardiano?


00:45:14.820 --> 00:45:16.820
- No, why?
- You don't know?


00:45:16.986 --> 00:45:18.379
She just got back from psych leave,


00:45:18.403 --> 00:45:20.587
she tried to kill herself,
she's never been able to deal...


00:45:20.611 --> 00:45:22.486
Alright. That's enough.


00:45:24.820 --> 00:45:25.986
Marcelin?


00:45:26.153 --> 00:45:27.713
Try to find a link between the Drocourts


00:45:27.861 --> 00:45:28.986
and the Vasseurs.


00:45:29.445 --> 00:45:30.837
From what I hear,
everyone knows everyone here.


00:45:30.861 --> 00:45:32.611
Yes, Inspector.


00:45:32.778 --> 00:45:33.861
Thank you, Marcelin.


00:45:37.361 --> 00:45:38.861
That was my boss.


00:45:39.570 --> 00:45:41.528
A stolen computer and the carcass of a dog


00:45:41.695 --> 00:45:43.570
isn't enough for a warrant
at the Vasseurs.


00:45:47.236 --> 00:45:48.903
Fuck, the computer.


00:46:01.237 --> 00:46:02.529
Fuck!


00:46:07.071 --> 00:46:08.196
Upstairs.


00:46:42.029 --> 00:46:44.696
Fuck. Fuck. Fucking shit.


00:46:48.321 --> 00:46:49.612
Stop!


00:46:52.779 --> 00:46:53.904
Stop!


00:46:58.279 --> 00:46:59.946
Stop! I said, 'Stop!'


00:47:00.112 --> 00:47:02.237
Stop or I will shoot you.


00:47:32.947 --> 00:47:34.405
Stop now!


00:48:02.780 --> 00:48:04.072
Stop!


00:48:04.405 --> 00:48:05.905
Stop!


00:48:27.072 --> 00:48:29.072
Stop or I'll shoot.


00:50:48.949 --> 00:50:52.157
THE INVISIBLE WORLD
SOUL EATER


00:51:11.240 --> 00:51:14.115
In order for the monster to die,


00:51:14.282 --> 00:51:17.615
man must perish
to invoke the clemency of heaven


00:51:17.782 --> 00:51:20.032
and its infamous justice.


00:51:20.199 --> 00:51:23.074
For only tears of salt
will repel the appetite


00:51:23.240 --> 00:51:24.574
of the Soul Eater.


00:51:25.782 --> 00:51:28.115
Time marches on,


00:51:28.282 --> 00:51:29.782
but legends remain.


00:51:29.949 --> 00:51:31.240
Pardon?


00:51:31.408 --> 00:51:32.908
The Soul Eater.


00:51:33.658 --> 00:51:35.450
He's an old local story.


00:51:35.616 --> 00:51:39.033
A story that's been passed down
from generation to generation.


00:51:39.950 --> 00:51:42.241
But what does that have
to do with your case?


00:51:42.408 --> 00:51:45.158
I don't know, but it keeps coming back
to this legend.


00:51:46.116 --> 00:51:47.866
Behind every victim,


00:51:48.033 --> 00:51:50.575
there's a person
who's inspired by this book.


00:51:50.741 --> 00:51:55.283
So in your opinion, a resident
of Roquenoir must be the Soul Eater?


00:51:57.033 --> 00:51:58.950
Perhaps.


00:52:04.158 --> 00:52:05.783
But if you knew,


00:52:06.825 --> 00:52:08.991
you would tell me, wouldn't you, Father?


00:52:10.575 --> 00:52:14.450
It's late and I'm quite tired, Inspector.


00:52:18.866 --> 00:52:20.366
Good night, Father.


00:52:23.908 --> 00:52:26.788
The funeral
for the pilot of the small tourist plane


00:52:26.866 --> 00:52:29.366
that crashed in the Vallee
de Gernon two weeks ago,


00:52:29.533 --> 00:52:32.158
was held today at the local cemetery.


00:52:32.325 --> 00:52:34.908
The ceremony was
an extremely private affair


00:52:35.075 --> 00:52:37.783
as the identity of the man
has not yet been confirmed.


00:52:38.283 --> 00:52:41.116
Investigators are reminding the public
that as not all the debris


00:52:41.283 --> 00:52:43.200
from the crash has been recovered,


00:52:43.366 --> 00:52:46.616
the search could resume at the
request of the authorities,


00:52:46.783 --> 00:52:48.241
which would represent the last hope


00:52:48.408 --> 00:52:50.491
of discovering the reason
the small plane went down.


00:52:50.658 --> 00:52:54.575
In other news, the president
will be travelling to...


00:53:01.034 --> 00:53:02.701
Fuck, Franck. You okay?


00:53:03.826 --> 00:53:06.159
Yeah, sorry, it's been crazy since
I got here.


00:53:06.326 --> 00:53:07.846
Yeah, well, I was starting to worry.


00:53:08.326 --> 00:53:10.784
So, get any leads from the van?


00:53:10.951 --> 00:53:13.191
No, nothing really, but I think
I'm in the right place.


00:53:13.242 --> 00:53:14.576
Why do you say that?


00:53:14.742 --> 00:53:16.451
Got my hands on a hard drive.


00:53:16.617 --> 00:53:19.117
There are encrypted files,
folders with links attached.


00:53:19.284 --> 00:53:20.968
It's all been coded.
I'll send you everything.


00:53:20.992 --> 00:53:22.117
I want notes on it.


00:53:22.284 --> 00:53:23.284
Can you do that?


00:53:23.409 --> 00:53:25.326
Sure. Let me see what I can do.


00:53:25.909 --> 00:53:27.659
Okay.


00:53:38.201 --> 00:53:40.701
So what's the deal with that cigarette?


00:53:44.117 --> 00:53:45.284
Here.


00:53:45.451 --> 00:53:47.367
I asked Marcelin to print up everything


00:53:47.534 --> 00:53:48.701
we had in the file.


00:53:48.867 --> 00:53:50.367
Interviews with witnesses,


00:53:50.534 --> 00:53:52.159
telephone records of the victims,


00:53:52.326 --> 00:53:53.576
maybe it could help you.


00:53:53.742 --> 00:53:54.784
Great, thanks.


00:53:56.451 --> 00:53:59.326
Now what's the deal
with that cigarette of yours?


00:54:00.326 --> 00:54:02.951
When those kids started disappearing,


00:54:03.117 --> 00:54:04.784
I was supposed to quit smoking.


00:54:06.409 --> 00:54:08.492
This was supposed to be my last one.


00:54:10.492 --> 00:54:12.909
I'm gonna light it when I close the case.


00:54:16.242 --> 00:54:17.409
I look at them every day.


00:54:20.076 --> 00:54:21.493
The hardest thing


00:54:22.035 --> 00:54:23.243
is seeing their smile.


00:54:25.202 --> 00:54:28.410
Despite all the pain and the suffering
of their disappearance,


00:54:28.577 --> 00:54:30.657
parents always choose
a picture of their kid smiling.


00:54:31.993 --> 00:54:33.452
Franck.


00:54:33.618 --> 00:54:36.452
The probabilities of finding a minor
after 48 hours


00:54:36.618 --> 00:54:37.952
are virtually nil.


00:54:38.118 --> 00:54:40.243
- So after six months...
- We're not looking for kids,


00:54:40.410 --> 00:54:41.450
we're looking for corpses.


00:54:44.410 --> 00:54:46.160
All the parents know that.


00:54:46.702 --> 00:54:48.660
But we all need to understand.


00:54:50.160 --> 00:54:53.660
We need to know
what happened and who hurt them.


00:54:54.118 --> 00:54:55.660
Who would do that?


00:54:56.535 --> 00:54:59.535
These parents just need to...


00:54:59.702 --> 00:55:01.452
bury their children.


00:55:04.327 --> 00:55:06.202
You got any children?


00:55:18.868 --> 00:55:20.493
I had a girl.


00:55:22.743 --> 00:55:25.160
I knew she was being bullied at school.


00:55:25.327 --> 00:55:26.910
But I was always working.


00:55:27.077 --> 00:55:29.202
And didn't listen to her enough.


00:55:32.243 --> 00:55:34.368
That morning, I,


00:55:34.535 --> 00:55:37.243
I knew immediately
that something wasn't right.


00:55:39.118 --> 00:55:41.202
Because she hugged me.


00:55:41.368 --> 00:55:43.743
Right before I left,
she gave me a big hug.


00:55:44.535 --> 00:55:47.786
And she always hated hugging
even when she was a little girl.


00:55:49.786 --> 00:55:52.328
It's as if I knew something horrible
was gonna happen,


00:55:52.494 --> 00:55:53.494
and I...


00:55:54.494 --> 00:55:56.036
I left anyway.


00:56:04.078 --> 00:56:05.661
Do you have any children?


00:56:06.536 --> 00:56:07.536
No.


00:56:08.578 --> 00:56:10.078
I'll top you up.


00:56:10.244 --> 00:56:11.661
Shit!


00:56:11.828 --> 00:56:13.911
Hang on. I'll take that.


00:56:26.328 --> 00:56:27.369
What?


00:56:28.161 --> 00:56:31.036
Maublanc, the guy who found
the carpenter's body,


00:56:31.578 --> 00:56:33.679
didn't he tell us that he called
the sawmill a few times


00:56:33.703 --> 00:56:36.244
before going over there
and that he left messages?


00:56:36.411 --> 00:56:38.451
Yeah, he said he ordered some planks
or something.


00:56:38.578 --> 00:56:40.328
He was lying through his teeth.


00:56:41.036 --> 00:56:43.453
There are no calls on the phone records.


00:56:44.953 --> 00:56:47.078
Hail Mary, full of grace.


00:56:47.244 --> 00:56:48.744
The Lord is with thee.


00:56:48.911 --> 00:56:50.369
Blessed art through among women


00:56:50.536 --> 00:56:52.953
and blessed is the fruit
of thy womb, Jesus.


00:56:53.119 --> 00:56:55.078
Holy Mary, mother of God,


00:56:55.244 --> 00:56:56.328
pray for us sinners.


00:56:56.494 --> 00:56:59.036
Now and at the hour of our death, amen.


00:56:59.203 --> 00:57:01.203
Hail Mary, full of grace.


00:57:01.369 --> 00:57:04.453
The Lord is with thee,
blessed are thou among women


00:57:04.619 --> 00:57:06.453
and blessed is the fruit
of thy womb, Jesus


00:58:07.620 --> 00:58:09.662
Holy Mary, mother of God.


00:58:09.829 --> 00:58:11.245
Pray for us sinners.


00:58:11.412 --> 00:58:12.954
Now and in the hour of our death...


00:58:17.662 --> 00:58:19.329
Go around the back.


00:59:10.621 --> 00:59:12.746
My God.


00:59:13.538 --> 00:59:15.413
Fuck.


00:59:34.580 --> 00:59:35.955
- Elisabeth!
- Franck!


00:59:36.121 --> 00:59:38.038
Stay with me. C'mon.


00:59:38.663 --> 00:59:39.746
Stay with me.


00:59:39.913 --> 00:59:42.455
Franck! Franck!


00:59:56.038 --> 00:59:57.330
Franck, come here!


00:59:57.496 --> 00:59:59.621
Elisabeth! Hey!


01:00:48.622 --> 01:00:50.289
My guys are with de Roland.


01:00:50.456 --> 01:00:52.206
They're taking him back to the hotel.


01:00:53.206 --> 01:00:55.622
He's strong, he'll be fine.


01:00:55.789 --> 01:00:57.872
Did you find Maublanc's computer?


01:00:58.039 --> 01:00:59.456
Yeah, Gonnet picked it up.


01:01:00.872 --> 01:01:02.247
That's great.


01:01:02.414 --> 01:01:04.956
Five violent deaths in two days.


01:01:05.747 --> 01:01:07.372
People are gonna start to panic.


01:01:08.247 --> 01:01:09.664
Ever seen anything like this?


01:01:10.956 --> 01:01:12.956
- No.
- This is a quiet little town.


01:01:13.122 --> 01:01:14.872
It's not like Paris or Marseille.


01:01:27.165 --> 01:01:28.748
Marcelin?


01:01:33.623 --> 01:01:35.332
The Maublancs had a kid?


01:01:35.498 --> 01:01:37.707
Yes, a daughter. Jeanne.


01:01:38.290 --> 01:01:39.873
Where is she?


01:01:40.915 --> 01:01:42.373
Start a search for her.


01:01:42.540 --> 01:01:44.040
Yes, Inspector.


01:03:33.708 --> 01:03:37.624
'He devours, he consumes
the value of innocence.


01:03:38.083 --> 01:03:41.083
From the destiny of souls,
he nourishes his power.


01:03:41.249 --> 01:03:43.874
Do not invite him in,
lest he invades your home.


01:03:44.041 --> 01:03:47.583
Do not answer him anything,
do not fall into his void.


01:03:47.749 --> 01:03:49.833
For it is under the skin of those you love


01:03:49.999 --> 01:03:51.958
that the monster resides.'


01:05:20.500 --> 01:05:24.167
All these murders were committed
in such violent unheard of ways


01:05:24.334 --> 01:05:25.459
that almost defy logic.


01:05:25.625 --> 01:05:27.000
The blows were all post-mortem.


01:05:27.167 --> 01:05:29.667
The man all ejaculated
in the throes of the act,


01:05:29.834 --> 01:05:32.250
and I even found vaginal
secretions with Ms. Vasseur.


01:05:32.959 --> 01:05:35.625
The one that sticks out is Ms. Maublanc.


01:05:36.667 --> 01:05:38.667
She never struck back at her husband.


01:05:39.376 --> 01:05:41.835
So what is it? Regular people
who suddenly go crazy?


01:05:42.001 --> 01:05:43.626
I have no other explanation.


01:05:43.793 --> 01:05:45.543
And the blood samples from the Vasseurs?


01:05:45.710 --> 01:05:47.918
- Not in yet.
- And I just sent out the ones


01:05:48.085 --> 01:05:49.585
from the recent victims.


01:05:49.918 --> 01:05:51.460
What about on your end, Marcelin?


01:05:52.293 --> 01:05:56.293
We found no evidence that there was
a third person at the crime scene.


01:05:56.460 --> 01:05:58.835
But Gonnet's working
on Maublanc's hard drive.


01:05:59.001 --> 01:06:01.168
Yeah, don't worry,
this one won't go missing.


01:06:01.335 --> 01:06:02.793
It's in a safe place.


01:06:02.960 --> 01:06:04.168
I'm gonna make it talk.


01:06:05.460 --> 01:06:07.543
What about the figurines?


01:06:08.251 --> 01:06:09.626
Where did you find this one?


01:06:10.376 --> 01:06:12.710
- At the Maublanc's.
- Their daughter Jeanne makes them.


01:06:12.876 --> 01:06:14.501
She's quite gifted.


01:06:14.668 --> 01:06:17.626
She seems to be fascinated
with the Soul Eater.


01:06:18.376 --> 01:06:20.144
If there really is
someone out there doing this,


01:06:20.168 --> 01:06:21.585
he'd know and use her figurines.


01:06:22.210 --> 01:06:23.793
Where is she now?


01:06:24.335 --> 01:06:25.335
We don't know.


01:06:26.585 --> 01:06:27.793
How long now?


01:06:27.960 --> 01:06:28.960
Since last night,


01:06:29.085 --> 01:06:30.126
we called her school


01:06:30.293 --> 01:06:31.376
and they confirmed that...


01:06:31.543 --> 01:06:33.543
She was there yesterday, but...


01:06:33.710 --> 01:06:34.710
but not last night.


01:06:36.460 --> 01:06:37.918
And what if he's real?


01:06:38.085 --> 01:06:39.460
Yeah, right.


01:06:39.626 --> 01:06:41.751
What if the Soul Eater really does exist?


01:06:42.376 --> 01:06:43.918
He's got a point.


01:06:45.335 --> 01:06:47.918
All these deaths aren't part
of some legend.


01:06:50.376 --> 01:06:52.793
And it's your soul that's being devoured
by this thing.


01:06:53.793 --> 01:06:55.793
That invisible part of yourself.


01:06:55.960 --> 01:06:57.543
Your subconscious.


01:06:58.751 --> 01:07:00.251
And it takes control of you.


01:07:01.168 --> 01:07:03.544
And clearly, we're dealing
with a loss of control, no?


01:07:04.252 --> 01:07:06.919
Well, what I saw yesterday
was more than that.


01:07:12.461 --> 01:07:14.002
Evan's not at the hospital.


01:07:15.002 --> 01:07:16.544
He disappeared.


01:07:16.711 --> 01:07:18.511
- Since when?
- Since last night.


01:07:19.836 --> 01:07:21.211
I looked everywhere.


01:07:21.377 --> 01:07:23.711
I thought he'd go and...
never found him.


01:07:26.044 --> 01:07:28.711
You know, Evan is,
well, he's very unstable.


01:07:29.086 --> 01:07:30.752
Alone out there, he...


01:07:30.919 --> 01:07:32.544
he might be a danger to himself


01:07:32.711 --> 01:07:35.294
- and to others.
- A little background, please.


01:07:37.169 --> 01:07:39.752
In the past, the principal
of Roquenoir School


01:07:39.919 --> 01:07:42.336
filed a report that there may
have been some abuse.


01:07:43.211 --> 01:07:47.169
When I first met Evan, he was six,
I think, yeah, he was six years old.


01:07:47.336 --> 01:07:50.461
And I saw right away that he was
the victim of violence.


01:07:51.752 --> 01:07:55.586
So I reported it immediately
to Child Protection,


01:07:55.752 --> 01:07:57.836
they launched an investigation,


01:07:58.002 --> 01:07:59.002
but never found anything.


01:07:59.127 --> 01:08:00.836
So they closed the file.


01:08:01.211 --> 01:08:02.627
Did you know Mr. and Ms. Vasseur?


01:08:02.794 --> 01:08:05.544
They had a real problem.


01:08:06.461 --> 01:08:08.836
They could never accept
the fact that their child needed


01:08:09.002 --> 01:08:10.711
to be in a structured environment.


01:08:11.336 --> 01:08:14.169
Fortunately, I could
continue my sessions with him.


01:08:14.336 --> 01:08:16.002
It was a constant battle.


01:08:16.169 --> 01:08:18.377
And the Soul Eater, do you have any idea


01:08:18.544 --> 01:08:20.419
why Evan is constantly talking about it?


01:08:22.044 --> 01:08:24.461
Well, his interpretation of this legend


01:08:24.627 --> 01:08:28.253
would allow him some protection from the
violence he sustained from his parents.


01:08:30.795 --> 01:08:34.837
He, kind of saw them
as the incarnation of harm.


01:08:35.837 --> 01:08:38.712
To escape from reality.


01:08:39.087 --> 01:08:41.253
He could just chase
their image from his mind.


01:08:41.962 --> 01:08:43.837
It's a survival mechanism.


01:08:44.628 --> 01:08:47.003
Do you think he can
manifest that into other people?


01:08:47.170 --> 01:08:48.337
Yes, it's possible.


01:08:48.878 --> 01:08:51.378
Do you know a young girl
named Jeanne Maublanc?


01:08:51.545 --> 01:08:54.378
Yes. She goes to the same
school as Evan where I work.


01:08:55.462 --> 01:08:56.462
Why do you ask?


01:08:56.628 --> 01:08:57.896
Because she disappeared as well.


01:08:57.920 --> 01:08:59.503
Wait a minute.


01:08:59.670 --> 01:09:01.503
You're also the school psychologist?


01:09:01.670 --> 01:09:03.462
Yes, well, you see how it is.


01:09:03.628 --> 01:09:04.837
It's a medical void here.


01:09:08.712 --> 01:09:09.920
Excuse me.


01:09:13.420 --> 01:09:16.920
And do... Do you know if Jeanne
and Evan know each other?


01:09:17.587 --> 01:09:19.378
I'm afraid not.


01:09:19.545 --> 01:09:21.628
But please find them as fast as you can.


01:09:21.795 --> 01:09:23.045
This child needs help.


01:09:26.045 --> 01:09:29.021
Guardiano, you need to inform
me immediately when you shoot someone


01:09:29.045 --> 01:09:31.295
with your firearm. Is that understood?


01:09:31.878 --> 01:09:33.295
I'm sorry, Commissioner


01:09:33.462 --> 01:09:35.021
Stop, alright, Elisabeth?
We had an agreement.


01:09:35.045 --> 01:09:36.729
And you've been paying me
lip service from the start.


01:09:36.753 --> 01:09:37.920
You got no excuses.


01:09:38.087 --> 01:09:39.207
The other two crime scenes


01:09:39.295 --> 01:09:41.003
have similar components
to the kidnappings.


01:09:41.170 --> 01:09:43.045
I made it clear
you were not to get involved


01:09:43.212 --> 01:09:44.313
in any case involving minors.


01:09:44.337 --> 01:09:45.729
As of now, we're cutting our losses


01:09:45.753 --> 01:09:47.021
so get back here, that's an order!


01:09:47.045 --> 01:09:49.212
- Hannah, Hannah.
- Just listen to me, please.


01:09:50.212 --> 01:09:51.753
Shit.


01:09:52.963 --> 01:09:54.921
So Marcelin and his men
are looking for Evan.


01:09:55.796 --> 01:09:58.421
I just contacted the school principal
at Saint-Philomène.


01:09:58.588 --> 01:10:00.228
It's in the Valley, she's waiting for us.


01:10:00.379 --> 01:10:02.004
Elisabeth?


01:10:02.171 --> 01:10:03.171
You okay?


01:10:05.004 --> 01:10:07.046
Yeah, let's go.


01:10:16.254 --> 01:10:18.171
I wanna thank you for yesterday.


01:10:19.213 --> 01:10:22.129
I know it's hard to make the decision
to use your service weapon,


01:10:22.296 --> 01:10:23.296
but...


01:10:24.046 --> 01:10:26.088
Well, if you hadn't, I'd be...


01:10:26.421 --> 01:10:28.671
lying in the morgue right now,
keeping Vasseur company.


01:10:28.838 --> 01:10:29.963
Glove compartment.


01:10:30.129 --> 01:10:32.588
- What?
- Light's in the glove compartment.


01:10:34.088 --> 01:10:35.629
He's been following us.


01:10:35.796 --> 01:10:37.596
I saw him in town
but out here in the country,


01:10:37.754 --> 01:10:39.379
I just made him.


01:10:44.754 --> 01:10:46.254
Do it.


01:10:49.671 --> 01:10:51.421
Fuck!


01:11:07.546 --> 01:11:09.171
- You okay?
- Yeah.


01:11:09.754 --> 01:11:11.921
Stay here, I'll be right back.


01:13:14.423 --> 01:13:15.423
Where are they?


01:13:15.590 --> 01:13:17.298
The kids, what'd you do with them?


01:13:17.465 --> 01:13:19.256
What did you do with them?


01:13:19.423 --> 01:13:21.548
Tell me!


01:13:25.423 --> 01:13:27.465
Hey, hey, stop!


01:13:27.631 --> 01:13:28.715
Talk!


01:13:29.090 --> 01:13:30.756
Where are the children?


01:13:31.381 --> 01:13:34.131
I don't... I don't know
anything about the kids.


01:13:35.215 --> 01:13:37.965
You better talk to me.


01:13:42.965 --> 01:13:44.006
The Cessna.


01:13:44.173 --> 01:13:46.090
That Cessna that crashed.


01:13:46.715 --> 01:13:49.298
It wasn't a tourist plane.


01:13:49.465 --> 01:13:51.715
It was... It was a drug runner.


01:13:52.881 --> 01:13:55.798
I came here to retrieve the merchandise.


01:13:55.965 --> 01:13:59.006
Check my pocket, check my pocket.


